# Paths excluded from the squashfs at mksquashfs time (NOT uninstalled — the
# chroot keeps them; they just never enter the image). First-class in Ubuntu's
# live-build 3.0~a57 fork: lb_binary_rootfs passes `-wildcards -ef` with this
# file when it exists. Purpose: get every strain's ISO under GitHub's 2 GiB
# single-asset cap so releases ship ONE flashable file (balenaEtcher can't
# rejoin split parts).
#
# TRADE-OFF, decided consciously: Calamares unpacks this same squashfs, so
# installed systems also lack man pages / offline GNOME help / non-English
# locales. `man foo` says "No manual entry" (web docs exist); GNOME Yelp help
# is degraded; English stays intact. ~250-350 MiB for that is the deal.
#
# DO NOT exclude usr/share/doc/*/copyright — this distro redistributes
# GPL/LGPL binaries and shipping their licence/attribution files is a
# compliance REQUIREMENT, not polish. The doc/ patterns below therefore name
# specific junk (changelogs, NEWS, examples) instead of doc/*.
usr/share/man/*
# Locales: keep en* (the [a-d]/[f-z] split skips the whole e* range — that
# also spares eo/es/et/eu, an acceptable overshoot to keep the pattern simple
# and en* provably safe).
usr/share/locale/[a-d]*
usr/share/locale/[f-z]*
usr/share/help/*
usr/share/gnome/help/*
usr/share/doc/*/changelog*
usr/share/doc/*/NEWS*
usr/share/doc/*/examples
# Kernel headers (~175 MB, nearly all of /usr/src): build-time artifacts for
# compiling out-of-tree/DKMS modules. Nothing in a running desktop reads them,
# and they are only here as a Recommends of the HWE kernel metapackage. Anything
# that genuinely needs them (e.g. a DKMS driver build) apt-installs the matching
# linux-headers package itself — drivers/install-nvidia.sh already does, and apt
# pulls headers as a dependency of the driver package. Excluded from every
# strain: this is the difference between lowspec shipping as one flashable file
# and shipping as split .part files.
usr/src/*
# Offline speech-to-text acoustic models (~37 MB). This is speech RECOGNITION
# (voice input), NOT the accessibility text-to-speech path — screen readers go
# through speech-dispatcher + flite/espeak, both of which are deliberately left
# intact. Nothing in the shipped desktop invokes pocketsphinx by default.
usr/share/pocketsphinx/*
# AppStream software-catalogue metadata (~22 MB): a rebuildable cache for the
# software centre. Shipping a stale snapshot of it in the image buys nothing,
# and 22 MB is more headroom than the lowspec strain has under GitHub's 2 GiB
# single-asset cap — so it stays excluded.
#
# BUT: "regenerated on demand by appstreamcli refresh" was true of the mechanism
# and false of this distro, because NOTHING EVER DEMANDED IT. Stripping this
# directory removes the source data for every app icon, screenshot, description
# and star rating GNOME Software shows, and the shipped image had no step
# anywhere that rebuilt it. The result was reported as: "a lot of the icons in
# the app store is gone (the screenshots and the stars and a lot of other
# stuff)", along with apps that could not be installed — Software cannot offer
# what it has no metadata for.
#
# The fix is modes/update/systemd/system/refract-catalogue-warmup.service, which
# runs `distro-appstore warm` ONCE on the first booted, networked session and
# rebuilds all of it. Do not delete that unit and leave this exclude in place:
# the two only make sense together.
var/lib/swcatalog/*
